\paragraph{The features decide what the critic can read.}
\Cref{fig:lemma-check} checks the lemma on features FB learned by TD rather than on a least-squares fit.
Across the five processes, eight ranks and ten runs each, the gap the trained critic reads and the gap its backward features permit agree with correlation $0.99$ and the same sign in $99.8\%$ of the critics; the residual is the distance of the bootstrapped fixed point from the least-squares forward map, largest at the ranks where the gap is half kept.
Adding the one direction the features discard restores the gap exactly, for every reward (\cref{app:bottleneck-family}).
The failure is therefore entirely a matter of which directions the backward features span.

